    "# Quiz: Time Series Forecasting with Support Vector Regressor\n",
    "\n",
    "> **On Alps:** These are the questions of this lesson's pre-lecture and post-lecture quizzes, from the course's quiz app, with the answers the quiz app accepts."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Pre-lecture quiz"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-7-3-pre-1\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>SVM stands for</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Statistical Vector Machine</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. The S in SVM stands for Support, not Statistical.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Support Vector Machine</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. SVM stands for Support Vector Machine.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Statistical Vector Model</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. SVM stands for Support Vector Machine, not Statistical Vector Model.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-7-3-pre-2\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Which of these ML techniques is used to predict continuous values?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Clustering</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Regression is the technique used to predict continuous values.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Classification</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. In classification, an SVM acts as a boundary. Regression is what predicts continuous values.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Regression</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Regression is a supervised learning technique that predicts continuous values.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-7-3-pre-3\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Which of these models is popularly used for time series forecasting?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>ARIMA</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. ARIMA is a very successful method for forecasting time series data.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>K-Means Clustering</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. The model described as very successful for forecasting time series is ARIMA.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Logistic Regression</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. The model described as very successful for forecasting time series is ARIMA.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
