    "## Post-lecture quiz"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-7-3-post-1\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>By which of these methods does an SVR learn?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Finding the best fit hyperplane that has the maximum number of data points</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. SVR finds the best-fit line, called a hyperplane in SVM, that has the maximum number of data points.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Learning the probability distribution of the dataset</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. SVR learns by finding the best-fit hyperplane that has the maximum number of data points.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Finding clusters in the dataset</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. SVR is a regressor. It predicts continuous data by finding a best-fit line, not clusters.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-7-3-post-2\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>What is the purpose of a kernel in SVMs?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>To measure the accuracy of the model predictions</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Accuracy is checked with MAPE. A kernel moves the data into a space with more dimensions.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>To transform the dataset to a higher dimension space</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. A kernel moves the data into a space with more dimensions, so the data is easier to separate.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>To standardize the values of the dataset</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Putting the values in the range 0 to 1 is a separate step, done with MinMaxScaler. A kernel moves the data into a space with more dimensions.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-7-3-post-3\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Which of these models consider the non-linearity in the dataset?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Simple Linear Regression</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Non-linearity in the data cannot be mapped by linear models.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>ARIMA</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. ARIMA is a linear method, and linear models cannot map non-linearity in the data.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>SVR using RBF kernel</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. An SVR, like the one built here with the RBF kernel, can consider non-linearity in the data.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  }
